
=======================================================================
🚀 Functional Example of How to Compile an NLP Project with Nuitka
=======================================================================

1. Be in the project path to execute: 

```bash
    cd compile-me/NLP_example
```
2. Update dependencies: 

```bash
    uv sync
```
3 Compile the project: (--remove-output to remove intermediate files): 

`standalone: `

```bash
    uv run nuitka --standalone --include-package=spacy --spacy-language-model=en_core_web_sm main.py
```

`onefile: `

```bash
    uv run nuitka --onefile --include-package=spacy --spacy-language-model=en_core_web_sm main.py
```

The program should download NLTK resources the first time it runs (if they are not already globally installed). It should then process the text with NLTK and spaCy without errors.

